+## 4b. Post-push tracking hook (`ci-watch`)
+
+Git has no `post-push` hook, so pushes are tracked with a watcher: after
+pushing, run it and stay until every workflow for that commit is green. It
+polls the Runs API (zero CI minutes) and, on failure, prints a digest —
+failed workflow → failed job → failed steps → the error lines from the
+step log — so the loop can be closed without digging through the web UI.
+
+```bash
+npm run ci:watch            # track HEAD (the commit just pushed)
+npm run ci:watch -- <sha>   # track a specific commit
+git pp                      # repo-local alias: `git push` + watch HEAD
+```
+
+Exit codes: `0` all green · `1` workflow failed (digest printed) ·
+`2` watcher timed out · `3` runs cancelled/superseded (watch the newer SHA).
+`--rerun-failed` re-runs only failed jobs — for transient/infra flakes;
+real failures get fixed and re-pushed (repro locally first: each full
+retry bills ~14 mins).
+
+One-time setup per clone (repo-local, never touches global gitconfig):
+
+```bash
+git config alias.pp '!f() { git push "$@" && exec "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/scripts/ci-watch.sh"; }; f'
+```
+
+---
+
